status: accept
exit: 42
note: |
  Rebinding a place variable to a fresh instance, then reading a field.
  Content-addressing makes p.x <- e (in-place field mutation) impossible, so the
  ONLY coherent "mutation" is the handle swap: p <- .-> Pt {...} builds a new slot
  and points the cell at the new handle. This exercises that a place stays
  first-class through a `mut` cell: the section handle survives
  the round-trip through the f64 cell and p.x projects the new value: the
  cell keeps the section type.
